-- coa7-ch4.l4: Part 13 Chapter 4, Public companies and traded companies: additional requirements for AGMs
-- (ss 336 to 340B), lines 4279-4367 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4. Seams taken as inputs: `s 392` (coa8), `s 1121` (coa24), `s 153` (coa3).

§ `Part 13 Chapter 4 -- Public companies and traded companies: additional requirements for AGMs`

-- ---- s 336 Public companies and traded companies: annual general meeting ----------------------------------

-- The period of 6 months (public company) or 9 months (private traded company) "beginning with the day following its
-- accounting reference date": the last day is the day before the same day 6 (or 9) months later.
-- src:4281 | (1) Every public company must hold a general meeting as its annual general meeting in each period of 6 months beginning with the day following its accounting reference date (in addition to any other meetings held during that period).
@ref s 336(1) Public companies and traded companies: annual general meeting: public company (src:4281)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounting reference date` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 336(1) the annual general meeting was held in the period of 6 months` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public company must hold a general meeting as its annual general meeting"
    ELSE IF `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` AT LEAST `the accounting reference date` PLUS 1
            AND `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` AT MOST (`add months` (`the accounting reference date` PLUS 1) 6) MINUS 1
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in each period of 6 months beginning with the day following its accounting reference date" -- FORK F7

-- src:4282 | (1A) Every private company that is a traded company must hold a general meeting as its annual general meeting in each period of 9 months beginning with the day following its accounting reference date (in addition to any other meetings held during that period).
@ref s 336(1A) Public companies and traded companies: annual general meeting: private traded company (src:4282)
GIVEN `the company is a private company that is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounting reference date` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 336(1A) the annual general meeting was held in the period of 9 months` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company that is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every private company that is a traded company must hold a general meeting as its annual general meeting"
    ELSE IF `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` AT LEAST `the accounting reference date` PLUS 1
            AND `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` AT MOST (`add months` (`the accounting reference date` PLUS 1) 9) MINUS 1
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in each period of 9 months beginning with the day following its accounting reference date" -- FORK F7

-- src:4283 | (2) A company that fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A) as a result of giving notice under section 392 (alteration of accounting reference date)—
-- src:4284 | (a) specifying a new accounting reference date, and
-- src:4285 | (b) stating that the current accounting reference period or the previous accounting reference period is to be shortened,
-- src:4286 | shall be treated as if it had complied with subsection (1) if it holds a general meeting as its annual general meeting within 3 months of giving that notice.
@ref s 336(2) Public companies and traded companies: annual general meeting: altering the accounting reference date (src:4283-4286)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A) as a result of giving notice under section 392` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a new accounting reference date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the current accounting reference period or the previous accounting reference period is to be shortened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 336(2) the company is treated as having complied with subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A) as a result of giving notice under section 392`)
        OR (NOT `the notice specifies a new accounting reference date`)
        OR (NOT `the notice states that the current accounting reference period or the previous accounting reference period is to be shortened`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A) as a result of giving notice under section 392 (alteration of accounting reference date)— (a) specifying a new accounting reference date, and (b) stating that the current accounting reference period or the previous accounting reference period is to be shortened"
    ELSE IF `the day on which the general meeting was held as the annual general meeting` AT MOST `add months` `the day on which the notice was given` 3
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated as if it had complied with subsection (1) if it holds a general meeting as its annual general meeting within 3 months of giving that notice" -- FORK F7

-- src:4287 | (3) If a company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 336(3) Public companies and traded companies: annual general meeting: offence (src:4287)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 336(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1) or (1A), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4288 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:4289 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:4290 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 336(4) Public companies and traded companies: annual general meeting: penalty (src:4288-4290)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 336(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 337 Public companies and traded companies: notice of AGM ----------------------------------------------

-- src:4292 | (1) A notice calling an annual general meeting of a public company or a private company that is a traded company must state that the meeting is an annual general meeting.
@ref s 337(1) Public companies and traded companies: notice of AGM: statement that it is an AGM (src:4292)
GIVEN `the company is a public company or a private company that is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice calls an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the meeting is an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 337(1) the notice states that the meeting is an annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company or a private company that is a traded company`) OR (NOT `the notice calls an annual general meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice calling an annual general meeting of a public company or a private company that is a traded company"
    ELSE IF `the notice states that the meeting is an annual general meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state that the meeting is an annual general meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4293 | (2) An annual general meeting of a public company that is not a traded company may be called by shorter notice than that required by section 307(2) or by the company's articles (as the case may be), if all the members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting agree to the shorter notice.
@ref s 337(2) Public companies and traded companies: notice of AGM: shorter notice (src:4293)
GIVEN `the company is a public company that is not a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting agree to the shorter notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 337(2) the annual general meeting may be called by shorter notice` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company that is not a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An annual general meeting of a public company that is not a traded company" -- FORK F19
    ELSE IF `all the members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting agree to the shorter notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be called by shorter notice than that required by section 307(2) or by the company's articles (as the case may be), if all the members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting agree to the shorter notice" -- FORK F22 -- MARGINAL b

-- "more than 6 weeks before the meeting": the clear-day rule of s 360(1) applies to s 337(3), so more than 42 clear days.
-- src:4294 | (3) Where a notice calling an annual general meeting of a traded company is given more than 6 weeks before the meeting, the notice must include—
-- src:4295 | (a) if the company is a public company, a statement of the right under section 338 to require the company to give notice of a resolution to be moved at the meeting, and
-- src:4296 | (b) whether or not the company is a public company, a statement of the right under section 338A to require the company to include a matter in the business to be dealt with at the meeting.
@ref s 337(3) Public companies and traded companies: notice of AGM: statements of rights (src:4294-4296)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which notice calling the annual general meeting is given` IS A DATE
      `the day of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338 to require the company to give notice of a resolution to be moved at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338A to require the company to include a matter in the business to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 337(3) the notice includes the statements this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a notice calling an annual general meeting of a traded company is given more than 6 weeks before the meeting"
    ELSE IF `s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` `the day on which notice calling the annual general meeting is given` `the day of the annual general meeting` AT MOST 42
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notice calling an annual general meeting of a traded company is given more than 6 weeks before the meeting, the notice must include" -- MARGINAL a
         ELSE IF ((NOT `the company is a public company`) OR `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338 to require the company to give notice of a resolution to be moved at the meeting`)
                 AND `the notice includes a statement of the right under section 338A to require the company to include a matter in the business to be dealt with at the meeting`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice must include— (a) if the company is a public company, a statement of the right under section 338 ..., (b) whether or not the company is a public company, a statement of the right under section 338A" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 338 Public companies: members' power to require circulation of resolutions for AGMs --------------------

-- src:4299 | (2) A resolution may properly be moved at an annual general meeting unless—
-- src:4300 | (a) it would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise),
-- src:4301 | (b) it is defamatory of any person, or
-- src:4302 | (c) it is frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 338(2) Public companies: members' power to require circulation of resolutions for AGMs: a resolution that may properly be moved (src:4299-4302)
GIVEN `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is defamatory of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(2) the resolution may properly be moved at the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)`
        OR `the resolution is defamatory of any person`
        OR `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution may properly be moved at an annual general meeting unless— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4298 | (1) The members of a public company may require the company to give, to members of the company entitled to receive notice of the next annual general meeting, notice of a resolution which may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at that meeting.
@ref s 338(1) Public companies: members' power to require circulation of resolutions for AGMs (src:4298)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution may properly be moved at the annual general meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is intended to be moved at the next annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(1) the members may require the company to give notice of the resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a public company may require the company to give"
    ELSE IF (NOT `the resolution is intended to be moved at the next annual general meeting`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice of a resolution which may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at that meeting"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the resolution may properly be moved at the annual general meeting`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a resolution which may properly be moved" -- MARGINAL b

-- src:4303 | (3) A company is required to give notice of a resolution once it has received requests that it do so from—
-- src:4304 | (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting to which the requests relate (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares in the company held as treasury shares), or
-- src:4305 | (b) at least 100 members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting to which the requests relate and hold shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of at least £100.
-- src:4306 | See also section 153 (exercise of rights where shares held on behalf of others).
@ref s 338(3) Public companies: members' power to require circulation of resolutions for AGMs: the requests (src:4303-4306)
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(3) the company is required to give notice of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting (excluding treasury shares)`
        OR (`number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting and hold shares in the company` AT LEAST 100
            AND `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` AT LEAST `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the resolution at the annual general meeting and hold shares in the company` TIMES 100)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is required to give notice of a resolution once it has received requests that it do so from— (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights ... or (b) at least 100 members" -- MARGINAL a

-- (d) received not later than (i) 6 weeks before the AGM (42 clear days, s 360(1)) or (ii) if later, the time at which notice
-- of the meeting is given.
-- src:4307 | (4) A request—
-- src:4308 | (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form,
-- src:4309 | (b) must identify the resolution of which notice is to be given,
-- src:4310 | (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and
-- src:4311 | (d) must be received by the company not later than—
-- src:4312 | (i) 6 weeks before the annual general meeting to which the requests relate, or
-- src:4313 | (ii) if later, the time at which notice is given of that meeting.
@ref s 338(4) Public companies: members' power to require circulation of resolutions for AGMs: the request (src:4307-4313)
GIVEN `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request identifies the resolution of which notice is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the company received the request` IS A DATE
      `the day of the annual general meeting to which the requests relate` IS A DATE
      `the day on which notice of that meeting is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(4) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A request— (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form"
    ELSE IF `the request identifies the resolution of which notice is to be given`
            AND `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`
            AND (`s 360(2) the period of the specified length is satisfied` 42 `the day on which the company received the request` `the day of the annual general meeting to which the requests relate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 OR `the day on which the company received the request` AT MOST `the day on which notice of that meeting is given`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) must identify the resolution of which notice is to be given, (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and (d) must be received by the company not later than— (i) 6 weeks before the annual general meeting to which the requests relate, or (ii) if later, the time at which notice is given of that meeting" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 338A Traded companies: members' power to include other matters in business dealt with at AGM -----------

-- src:4316 | (2) A matter may properly be included in the business at an annual general meeting unless –
-- src:4317 | (a) it is defamatory of any person, or
-- src:4318 | (b) it is frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 338A(2) Traded companies: members' power to include other matters: a matter that may properly be included (src:4316-4318)
GIVEN `the matter is defamatory of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338A(2) the matter may properly be included in the business at the annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the matter is defamatory of any person` OR `the matter is frivolous or vexatious`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A matter may properly be included in the business at an annual general meeting unless – (a) it is defamatory of any person, or (b) it is frivolous or vexatious"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4315 | (1) The members of a traded company may request the company to include in the business to be dealt with at an annual general meeting any matter (other than a proposed resolution) which may properly be included in the business.
@ref s 338A(1) Traded companies: members' power to include other matters in business dealt with at AGM (src:4315)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a proposed resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter may properly be included in the business at the annual general meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338A(1) the members may request the company to include the matter in the business` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) OR `the matter is a proposed resolution`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a traded company may request the company to include in the business to be dealt with at an annual general meeting any matter (other than a proposed resolution)" -- FORK F19
    ELSE CONSIDER `the matter may properly be included in the business at the annual general meeting`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matter ... which may properly be included in the business" -- MARGINAL b

-- src:4319 | (3) A company is required to include such a matter once it has received requests that it do so from—
-- src:4320 | (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the meeting, or
-- src:4321 | (b) at least 100 members who have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of at least £100.
-- src:4322 | See also section 153 (exercise of rights where shares held on behalf of others).
@ref s 338A(3) Traded companies: members' power to include other matters: the requests (src:4319-4322)
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `number of requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338A(3) the company is required to include the matter` MEANS
    IF `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote at the meeting`
        OR (`number of requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company` AT LEAST 100
            AND `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` AT LEAST `number of requesting members who have a right to vote at the meeting and hold shares in the company` TIMES 100)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is required to include such a matter once it has received requests that it do so from— (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights ... or (b) at least 100 members" -- MARGINAL a

